+# Narrowing NG-9 for a Veterinarian Specialty Filter
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declared search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian out of scope, leaving only owners searchable. A request to filter the veterinarian directory by specialty tests the row's edge: filtering the directory by an attribute it already presents is not the free-text, paged prefix search NG-9 was written against, yet it touches the same "veterinarians are not searchable" boundary.
+
+The owner has decided the boundary (2026-08-23): narrow NG-9 rather than treat the request as reopening the whole row.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Leave NG-9 whole and decline the filter.** Rejected: the row's rationale is that repeating free-text prefix search elsewhere teaches nothing new. A whole-name filter on an already-shown attribute is a different, smaller capability the rationale does not cover.
+2. **Drop NG-9 and open veterinarian search generally.** Rejected: free-text veterinarian search would add surface without teaching a new pattern, exactly the cost the row records.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen): keep free-text veterinarian search out; bring filtering the directory by a specialty it already shows into scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 is narrowed. Free-text search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian stays out of scope. Filtering the veterinarian directory by a whole specialty name — on both the paged page and the reinstated JSON endpoint — is in scope, realized by REQ-VET-003. The reinstatement of the JSON endpoint as a supported surface is the enabling boundary change; the endpoint's prior withdrawn requirement, REQ-VET-002, stays withdrawn and its id is not reused.
+
+The filter is a URL contract only in this decision; a visible control is a separate, future decision.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation for its narrowed portion; free-text veterinarian search remains a non-goal.
+- The JSON endpoint gains standing as a supported surface, reversing its 2026-07-31 withdrawal without reviving REQ-VET-002.
+- A later request for free-text veterinarian search, or for a visible filter control, is its own recorded owner decision — this narrowing does not grant either.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [PRD REQ-VET-003](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the specialty filter the narrowing admits.
