 The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
 
+Either surface of the directory — the paged page and the machine-readable JSON endpoint — can be narrowed to the veterinarians holding one named specialty `[REQ-VET-003]`. The JSON endpoint, once withdrawn as an artifact nothing consumed, is a supported surface again, and this filter is its first capability. The filter is supplied only through the request URL, as an optional `specialty` value; neither surface gains a visible control — no form, dropdown, or other page control — in this requirement. A specialty is matched on its whole name, disregarding letter case, and not as a prefix. On the paged page the filter applies before paging, and the paging links carry the specialty forward so a narrowed result stays navigable across its pages. A value matching no veterinarian returns the ordinary page or JSON document with an empty veterinarian list, not an error, and a blank or whitespace-only value behaves as though no filter were given — exactly as an empty owner search does. Without the value, either surface behaves as it does today `[REQ-VET-003]`.
